  "meta": {
    "title": "Act 4 — The Seam",
    "note": "The finale of Bonds of Red (game-story.md §4, issue #146). Quest 1 ships (issue #162): the homecoming — the cast at the Encampment fire and the fork they send you down. The guardian quests (#163–#165) and the `seam` zone (#166) follow, one issue each.",
    "loading": "On `act-3-complete`, through ACT_PACKAGES in main.ts (issue #209): NOT at boot, because unlike the sea and the sky nothing of this act is part of the open world's geography — the act stages out of the Encampment, and its one new place is a zone entered in quest 5. Once loaded it stays for the session. The people it brings are placed by `Npcs.reconcile` the moment the definitions land.",
    "the-seam": "Given AND closed by npc:gain at the Encampment (core.json — an id is global and core may not depend on a package that arrives later, so his rows sit beside him). The prerequisite is the door for THIS quest; everything else in the act tests seam-known.",
    "choose-a-road": "DROPPED (issue #146 comment, option a). The spec's `choose-a-road` was to be satisfied by STARTING a guardian quest, but 2–4 name this quest as a prerequisite and a prerequisite means COMPLETED — the objective could never tick. The fork itself is the choice: Three Roads closes on hearing the four out, and the order of 2–4 is the player's.",
    "the-fire": "Four placements, one per recurring character (game-story.md §2 — one body, one name key, a talk list gated on flags), `present` on act-3-complete. They STAY for the act: Coil is at Kelphold and Pell in the Orrery at the same time, the way Gain is at three fires, and their lines after seam-known say which road each of them is waiting on.",
    "the-guardians": "Three bosses, one rhythm (`behaviour: guardian` in combat/enemies.ts) in three elements: `bond` names the mount kind that can hurt it AND how it moves — the walker on Stonewatch's drove ground, the swimmer under Maw's Rest, the flyer over the Orrery's open frame. Each quest tests its mount FLAG (§6) and the fight itself refuses anyone not in that saddle. Any order; each sets its `guardian-*-freed` thread."
  },
